a live context's facts are the facts its backend's name parses to: true
the facts bind a hardware grid exactly where the device bounds a workgroup's threads: true
codegen_capabilities.select_blend at f32 and f64 agrees with the select blend policy: true
on cc, codegen_capabilities.select_blend reports Blend_truth at f32 and f64 and None elsewhere: true
under with_select_blend ~blend:false, codegen_capabilities.select_blend answers None: true
grid_execution alone moves the GPU and CPU search-shaping key reads: true
workgroup_shared_placement alone moves whether a node may be kept off the device: true
the sketch, split and seeded-singles keys follow the sketch seeding fact: true
sinks_untuned_reductions alone moves whether the untuned sink key is read: true
queued_timing alone moves the queued batch depth cap: true
retries_contended_window alone moves the contended-window retry: true
host_load_attributable alone moves the dispersion policy: true
renders_lane_bounds_check alone moves whether a compile under the key owes the cc-only notice: true
